# SiteWise Flutter mobile — local development defines (SAMPLE / PLACEHOLDERS).
#
# Copy this file to `sitewise_dev.env` in this directory and fill in the values.
# `sitewise_dev.env` is git-ignored: it contains a Supabase PUBLISHABLE key.
# NEVER put the Supabase SECRET / service-role key in this file or any Flutter
# asset. The publishable key is designed for client builds; the secret key is
# server-only and already lives in backend/.env.
#
# Usage from the workspace root (C:\Users\Lenovo\AndroidStudioProjects\FYP):
#   flutter run -t fyp_mobile_app/lib/main.dart ^
#       --dart-define-from-file=fyp_mobile_app/config/sitewise_dev.env
#
# Android Studio: Run > Edit Configurations > main.dart > Additional run args:
#   --dart-define-from-file=$PROJECT_DIR$/fyp_mobile_app/config/sitewise_dev.env
#
# Start the unified backend from the workspace root FIRST:
#   .\run-sitewise.cmd              (loopback + automatic adb reverse)
#   .\run-sitewise.cmd -Mobile      (same, but fail if no device is attached)
#   .\run-sitewise.cmd -AllowLan    (bind 0.0.0.0 for a real LAN address)
#
# ---- Target-specific API hosts -------------------------------------------
# The backend serves BOTH the Jaspr frontend and /api/v1/* on ONE port, 8090.
# The old :8000 default belonged to the retired two-server launcher — nothing
# listens there when .\run-sitewise.cmd is used.
#
#   USB device (recommended): API_HOST_MODE=adb-reverse
#       -> http://127.0.0.1:8090 as seen from the DEVICE. Requires
#          `adb reverse tcp:8090 tcp:8090`, which the launcher sets up
#          automatically when a device is attached. No LAN IP needed.
#   Android emulator:        API_HOST_MODE=emulator
#       -> http://10.0.2.2:8090 (the emulator's alias for the host PC).
#   Same-subnet LAN device:  API_BASE_URL=http://<HOST-LAN-IP>:8090
#       -> start the backend with -AllowLan and allow Python inbound.
#
# An explicit API_BASE_URL always wins over API_HOST_MODE. Never bake a LAN
# IP into a committed Dart source file; keep it in this define file only.
# WEB_BASE_URL must be an origin the user's browser can open for email
# confirmation / password recovery; add it to the Supabase redirect allowlist.
#
# Starting .\run-sitewise.cmd does NOT rebuild Flutter. After changing any
# value here, stop and re-run the app so the defines are compiled in again.
#
# ---- Keys -----------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_REPLACE_ME
API_HOST_MODE=adb-reverse
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
WEB_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
